# This is the processing directive for uni-temporal Anchor Modeling in BigQuery
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
#
# BigQuery has no sequences, no unique constraints and no triggers, and its primary and foreign keys are not enforced;
# a dataset is its schema. It has no equivalence here (the table says so in SQL/Helpers.js).
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/BigQuery/NamingConvention.js
SQL/BigQuery/derive.js
SQL/BigQuery/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateAttributeRewinders.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateKeys.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateIntegrityChecks.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/AddDescriptions.sisula
